.TH CPN 1 "2026" "chopin 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpn \- copy files and directories (chopin under a shorter name)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpn
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fISOURCE\fR... \fIDEST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
cpn is the chopin binary under a shorter name; argv[0] changes nothing
but the diagnostic program name. Stub page until v0.1.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chopin (1),
.BR cp (1)
